    {
      "id": "the-third-part-of-king-henry-the-sixth/sceneII_14.3/p@67266",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "WARWICK.\nForspent with toil, as runners with a race,\nI lay me down a little while to breathe;\nFor strokes received, and many blows repaid,\nHave robbed my strong-knit sinews of their strength,\nAnd spite of spite, needs must I rest awhile.",
