      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "RICHARD.\nBrother, give me thy hand; and, gentle Warwick,\nLet me embrace thee in my weary arms.\nI, that did never weep, now melt with woe\nThat winter should cut off our spring-time so.",
