    },
    {
      "id": "the-third-part-of-king-henry-the-sixth/sceneII_14.3/p@70221",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "GEORGE.\nYet let us all together to our troops,\nAnd give them leave to fly that will not stay,\nAnd call them pillars that will stand to us;\nAnd if we thrive, promise them such rewards\nAs victors wear at the Olympian games.\nThis may plant courage in their quailing breasts,\nFor yet is hope of life and victory.\nForslow no longer; make we hence amain.",
